# --- Claude Code: publish only intended config/scripts, never runtime state ---
# Everything under ~/.claude is ignored by default (session transcripts, shell-env
# snapshots, cached auth tokens, plugins, backups, caches all live here); only the
# hand-maintained config + scripts below are whitelisted back in. Add new Claude
# config files explicitly (git add -f) so runtime state can never leak.
claude/.claude/*
!claude/.claude/settings.json
!claude/.claude/statusline.sh
!claude/.claude/tmux-limits.sh

# --- credentials: NEVER in this repo (belt; the pre-commit hook is the suspenders) ---
# Private keys / certs
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.gpg
id_rsa
id_ed25519
id_ecdsa
id_dsa
# Token / secret stores
**/rclone.conf
**/.credentials.json
**/credentials.json
**/.netrc
**/.git-credentials
**/*secret*
**/*token*
.env
.env.*
# Passphrase files. This gap is how restic/.config/restic/password reached a
# PUBLIC repo and stayed there from 2026-08-11 until it was noticed: the block
# above catches *secret* and *token* but nothing matching "password", and the
# restic repo passphrase is stored in a file named exactly that. restic wants a
# file it can read unattended (RESTIC_PASSWORD_FILE), so the file has to exist —
# it just must never be tracked. It lives at ~/.config/restic/password, outside
# any stow package now.
**/password
**/*password*
**/*passphrase*
!.env.example

# --- general junk ---
*.log
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Thunar rewrites this on every exit (keybinding accel cache) — not worth versioning
Thunar/.config/Thunar/accels.scm

# btop rewrites this on every exit (runtime state baked in) — not worth versioning
btop/.config/btop/btop.conf

# systemd writes these enablement links itself on `systemctl --user enable`, and
# their targets are absolute /home/<user>/... paths that resolve for one username.
# Which units to enable is recorded in kb3lyb-bootstrap (frameworkimage) instead.
systemd/.config/systemd/user/*.target.wants/

# --- NEVER publish: writing-voice profile -----------------------------------
# ~/.claude/mark-voice-guide.md is derived from ~1,400 private emails and would
# let someone impersonate Mark convincingly. Already covered by the deny-all on
# line 6, repeated here as the LAST word in the file so a future `!` whitelist
# cannot silently un-ignore it (last matching pattern wins). The pre-commit hook
# blocks it by filename too, in case someone reaches for `git add -f`.
claude/.claude/mark-voice-guide.md
**/mark-voice-guide.md
